@*
    CONNECTION STATUS - the plant feed's health, in the header on every page.

    This used to carry the operating-mode selector (SIMULATION / SIM · 46-TAG / LIVE). It was
    removed for go-live: a button that re-badges the feed has no place on a control-room screen
    operators are meant to trust. The mode now comes only from the data - whatever the source
    declares, recorded in FRAME.OP_MODE - and nothing in the UI can change it.

    What stays is the one question this chip answers: is a feed reaching us right now?
*@
@using Crm04.Web.Components.Common
@using Crm04.Web.State
@inject MillStore Mill

<span class="text-meta inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-semibold @(Healthy ? "text-healthy" : "text-alarm")">
    <Icon Name="@(Healthy ? "Wifi" : "WifiOff")" Size="15" />
    <span class="text-text-faint font-medium">SOURCE</span>
    @* STALE means a feed that was flowing and stopped. With no summary ever received there is
       nothing to be stale about, so say what is actually true. *@
    @(Mill.Summary is null ? "NO FEED" : Healthy ? "CONNECTED" : Stale ? "STALE" : "DISCONNECTED")
</span>

@code {
    private bool Stale => Mill.Summary?.Communication.Stale ?? true;
    private bool Healthy => (Mill.Summary?.Communication.Connected ?? false) && !Stale;
}
